<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Man convicted of arson over deadly 2025 Palisades fire in Los Angeles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a05940f95697ba3179b5c2df4da334e5b138a8b0fc4cc484978ef032b55e75ee</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T07:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/man-convicted-of-arson-over-deadly-2025-palisades-fire-in-los-angeles/a-80007933--9f183d2c9cc1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/man-convicted-of-arson-over-deadly-2025-palisades-fire-in-los-angeles/a-80007933?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A 30-year-old man has been convicted of causing one of the most destructive wildfires in the history of Los Angeles. The verdict came after the case was retried.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Three El Salvador soldiers die in explosives accident in Haiti</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca880d01f1eaaa1b52c70e0ac361a2cce6e5e23d68845383b5370355d9d1d9da</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T06:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-el-salvador-soldiers-die-in-explosives-accident-in-haiti/a-80008005--520475dc82ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-el-salvador-soldiers-die-in-explosives-accident-in-haiti/a-80008005?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The soldiers were part of a Salvadoran military contingent deployed to the violence-ridden Caribbean nation last month to rescue four missing airmen. The deployment has widened into an operation against Haiti's gangs.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil ex-President Jair Bolsonaro taken to hospital over abdominal pain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ae60fdd06fa3ca113367f8edc2e888e0481f75f3a0c0f4523360de9e9f49314</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T03:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-ex-president-jair-bolsonaro-taken-to-hospital-over-abdominal-pain/a-80007648--e735cc923d74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-ex-president-jair-bolsonaro-taken-to-hospital-over-abdominal-pain/a-80007648?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jair Bolsonaro has been hospitalized in Brasilia with intestinal obstruction. The former far-right Brazilian leader is receiving pain medications, his son Carlos said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK anti-migrant activist jailed for slashing Channel dinghy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecb4bbfd1bbbdf603974ca7dbbc980662e9f999b209aedc46be8514c5ef7163b</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T02:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-anti-migrant-activist-jailed-for-slashing-channel-dinghy/a-80007576--c3711b9c2af1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-anti-migrant-activist-jailed-for-slashing-channel-dinghy/a-80007576?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Daniel Thomas, known as "Danny Tommo," slashed a dinghy with a knife while a French rescue worker was on board. The incident was livestreamed to a large social media audience amid growing tensions over migrant crossings.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US judge approves Bayer's $7.25 billion cancer settlement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa148f56de7d3f9cd7ffec44990c710928f1c7061ecd8b6db69b798ef8b5fcc0</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T00:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-judge-approves-bayer-s-7-25-billion-cancer-settlement/a-80007474--2da6c68c9dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-judge-approves-bayer-s-7-25-billion-cancer-settlement/a-80007474?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayer could end years of costly lawsuits in the US over claims that its Roundup weedkiller causes cancer. Tens of thousands of people could now receive compensation, although some lawyers say the payments are too low.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian ornithologist jailed over small donations to Navalny's foundation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:803ea5b3857da0f74534ff380a42f7685c0d136d0826d18f3d5449022239a693</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505--49dba4e1f94e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-ornithologist-jailed-over-small-donations-to-navalny-s-foundation/a-80005505?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sofia Rosenfeld has devoted her life to studying Arctic birds. A Russian court sentenced her to 3.5 years in a penal colony over donations to Navalny's foundation. Friends and family are fighting for her release.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Repression against Iranian lawyers increases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db4cb8c8ec3b1f10c1fba59c78c221be29a17bba13956bc7193cbd297f33f936</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/repression-against-iranian-lawyers-increases/a-80006742--c2e9244e707c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/repression-against-iranian-lawyers-increases/a-80006742?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 135 lawyers in Iran have been subjected to repressive measures over the past year. UN experts warn that this seriously jeopardizes the right of those accused to trial in a constitutional court.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>At COP31, conflict over climate science slows action on global warming</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4136e8f46cb1f111385cd26a1c992affb6a2259f90c0b769f7031deba6bbc78e</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-cop31-conflict-over-climate-science-slows-action-on-global-warming/a-80004894--9b014bd32e3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-cop31-conflict-over-climate-science-slows-action-on-global-warming/a-80004894?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Attacks on climate science and disinformation risk delaying key measures at COP31 in Antalya. As the UN climate talks draw to a close, how will that affect efforts to come to an agreement?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: UN Climate summit enters final phase with no deal in sight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db368272f761f530843b5ebf30aec9886dbb75893b5375c9d66e7eca1a1d802c</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-un-climate-summit-enters-final-phase-with-no-deal-in-sight/live-79999516--9cd590b81239.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-un-climate-summit-enters-final-phase-with-no-deal-in-sight/live-79999516?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After nearly two weeks of negotiations, countries remain divided on how to fight global warming. A new draft declaration doesn't mention the phaseout of fossil fuels, the main drivers of climate change. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Has the 'Parthenon puzzle' been solved? The long quest to reassemble lost eastern pediment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca7766f8a8cfe65f19a5d18382be2c8ce103bc4d69709eee55822f5f707a20b2</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098--4f23b2ccbfc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The depiction of the birth of the goddess Athena above the Parthenon's entrance is considered a masterpiece of ancient art. Now, a German research team has pieced together all the surviving fragments.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Kids take to streets over school, climate and costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:976d6449c2db73f380ccad3bfe937bbdaae78a58f77db5c34a7fbb1427aa49dd</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T17:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-kids-take-to-streets-over-school-climate-and-costs/live-79998529--8437273d8ab1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-kids-take-to-streets-over-school-climate-and-costs/live-79998529?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thousands of young people turned out across Germany demanding improvements in education, climate and affordability. Protesters say they aren't being taken seriously and will keep protesting until things change.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine updates: Russian attack 'one of largest,' Zelenskyy says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc4ec46be2893fe6daecb5f2fcc376ffce091a8519dd4a055c9eb2106980aeaa</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T17:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-russian-attack-one-of-largest-zelenskyy-says/live-79999822--2e1dfbc4ab78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-russian-attack-one-of-largest-zelenskyy-says/live-79999822?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy said Russia launched one of the largest aerial attacks since the invasion began. Poland accused Moscow of a "provocation," saying two missiles landed in the NATO country.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Better educated than ever — yet Germany's Gen Z is being shut out of its own future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e63f17883d69108a4b42977b19cb1d9bd678feb4e3e8223ebadbe1ddd4b9c30</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T17:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/better-educated-than-ever-yet-germany-s-gen-z-is-being-shut-out-of-its-own-future/a-80005823--59d88b978f2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/better-educated-than-ever-yet-germany-s-gen-z-is-being-shut-out-of-its-own-future/a-80005823?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Never before have young people faced so many challenges. Young Germans are asking: Will I be better off than my parents later in life?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Can German auto manufacturing recover after Mercedes and VW cuts?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea7283162a1d72a227bf2c93c8b122d5e35b791ff264512a2567ea07f5312e26</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-german-auto-manufacturing-recover-after-mercedes-and-vw-cuts/a-79946928--88277c189f1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-german-auto-manufacturing-recover-after-mercedes-and-vw-cuts/a-79946928?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German automakers are pulling back on investments at home, sparking fresh anxiety about the auto sector's future. Some industry watchers think there is still a narrow window to stem the decline. But how?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Measles in America: Here's a constructive approach to beating the disease, based on Brazil's experience</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10dc553e0a85ad34698222aef1b70c8c977e650bd1f7715abb831b68daf47fde</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/measles-in-america-here-s-a-constructive-approach-to-beating-the-disease-based-on-brazil-s-experienc/a-79990626--11abc405874e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/measles-in-america-here-s-a-constructive-approach-to-beating-the-disease-based-on-brazil-s-experience/a-79990626?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is now officially a measles contagion zone. By mid-2026, there were more infections than in all of the previous year. But the country could beat measles again, just like Brazil did two years ago.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Is Pakistan backing anti-Taliban groups in Afghanistan?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8dd5d76cf33fa21024e2b0f7ff093d9490d3f7d2a3338f011e21f2c9ba60af3</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814--1a7b1c3175b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-pakistan-backing-anti-taliban-groups-in-afghanistan/a-80004814?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Taliban rulers in Afghanistan have accused Pakistan of aiding and sheltering armed resistance groups. The allegations come amid heightened tensions and are likely to deepen the rift between the two neighbors.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany face belgium in Nations League quarterfinals — Klopp plays down favorites tag</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7be7875e7fe7accfdd634856302ddbdad9d98eadf475a226c997daebd43956a2</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-face-belgium-in-nations-league-quarterfinals-klopp-plays-down-favorites-tag/a-80004794--66b2cbbf524d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-face-belgium-in-nations-league-quarterfinals-klopp-plays-down-favorites-tag/a-80004794?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp is looking to "carry positive momentum forward" as his team draw neighboring Belgium in the quarterfinals of the UEFA Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU and UK strike 'landmark deal' to strengthen ties after Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02a114ded39193531a023854eadd0fd9e16f638486e6ca477a6b3c553ee71014</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-and-uk-strike-landmark-deal-to-strengthen-ties-after-brexit/a-80001076--f12586fcea84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-and-uk-strike-landmark-deal-to-strengthen-ties-after-brexit/a-80001076?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union and the United Kingdom have agreed on "landmark" deals on youth mobility and trade. Leaders on both sides praised the agreement as they seek to rebuild ties.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey takes control of opposition broadcaster Sozcu TV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61260c3c33e01a414896624be28a99d8de5635cbb725fd1ccff35dc7f8b3189b</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-takes-control-of-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv/a-80001984--d9f6e0119d22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-takes-control-of-opposition-broadcaster-sozcu-tv/a-80001984?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the latest in a series of raids and arrests, another major pro-opposition Turkish broadcaster has been brought under state control. This is the third in a year.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Africa at COP31: Will climate cash finally flow?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36ffa818af23249d3f9b84c4274cdf871249eb612e395a66c49e60dc44095d9d</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-at-cop31-will-climate-cash-finally-flow/a-80002269--5d2b279256b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-at-cop31-will-climate-cash-finally-flow/a-80002269?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the curtains draw to a close on COP31 in Antalya, one question looms large for African countries: Will climate promises finally translate into the funding African communities need to cope with a warming world?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar genocide ruling: Rohingya say struggle for justice not over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a2b6e9761bd0ec7811588ce4dfc390aa591c977ed265bc3361b78aaee52396a</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-genocide-ruling-rohingya-say-struggle-for-justice-not-over/a-80003365--347a55d37759.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-genocide-ruling-rohingya-say-struggle-for-justice-not-over/a-80003365?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ICJ has held Myanmar responsible for genocide against the Rohingya and ordered restitution and reparations. Community members have hailed the ruling, but caution that achieving real change will be long and hard.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
